title: Palo Alto Networks: High availability state
agents: paloalto_api
catalog: hw/network/paloalto
license: GPLv2
distribution: checkmk-paloalto-api
description:
 Monitors the high availability state of a firewall that is part of an HA
 pair. The service is OK if the local member is active or passive (or
 active-primary/active-secondary for active/active), WARN for initial or
 tentative and CRIT for suspended, non-functional and other states. The peer
 state and the peer connection are checked the same way. A configuration that
 is not synchronized results in WARN by default. Optionally an expected local
 state can be configured to detect an unplanned failover.

discovery:
 One service is created if HA is enabled on the firewall.
